{
  "description": "The order of every channel list. `sort` (absent means `newest`) is the chosen order; `expected` is the ids in order. In every sort the channels that are off (`enabled` false, whatever they have) go last, by name. By name means: by `title` ignoring case exactly as the feed's `title` sort compares titles (shared/fixtures/feed-order.json), then by `id` (ASCII). `newest`: channels that are on and have at least one fetched item come first, by the `publishedAt` of their newest fetched item, newest first (RFC 3339 UTC strings compared as plain ASCII strings), ties by name; then channels that are on with nothing fetched (`newest` absent), by name. Every fetched item counts, whether or not it passes the channel's filter and whether or not it is watched. `name`: the channels that are on, by name, fetched or not. `unwatched`: the channels that are on by `unwatched` (how many of the channel's unwatched fetched items pass its filter; absent means 0), most first, ties in `newest` order. `newestUnwatched`: the channels that are on and have at least one unwatched item come first (`newestUnwatched` present: the `publishedAt` of the newest of the items `unwatched` counts, so it is present exactly when that count is above 0), by it, newest first, however many they are, ties in `newest` order; then the channels that are on with nothing unwatched, in `newest` order. It is the order of the Mac and web sidebars, which offer no other, and it is not a value of the synced `channelSort` setting (shared/fixtures/settings.json), which stays `newest`, `name` or `unwatched`: no chip offers it and a phone's list is never in it. The chips at the top of the feed change neither the counts nor the order; the channel list's own chips (shared/fixtures/channel-chips.json) choose which channels are listed and change neither.",
